# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate carries the time evolution $e^{-itH}$ of a whole operator. A fermion-to-fermion synthesis rewrites that gate into a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") of smaller fermionic gates. Both sides of the rewrite stay in fermionic space, which is what distinguishes it from the fermion-to-qubit synthesis that follows: the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) survive it, whereas a fermion-to-qubit mapping returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), which has no concept of grouping.\n"
msgstr "Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") membawa evolusi waktu $e^{-itH}$ dari seluruh operator. Sintesis fermion-ke-fermion menulis ulang gate itu menjadi [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") berisi gate fermionik yang lebih kecil. Kedua sisi penulisan ulang tetap berada di ruang fermionik, dan inilah yang membedakannya dari sintesis fermion-ke-qubit yang menyusul: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") milik operator (lihat [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)) tetap bertahan, sedangkan pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit mengembalikan [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), yang tidak mengenal konsep pengelompokan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two knobs select the method. `Evolution.synthesis` sets it on one gate, and the [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") transpiler pass sets it across a whole circuit. Both take an [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), the interface any such rewrite implements. The methods this package currently provides for an evolution are product formulas, which is what the rest of this guide uses: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") for a first-order formula (the default) and [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") for a higher even order. Anything else implementing the interface is selected the same way, and the sections on the two knobs apply to it unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Dua pengaturan menentukan metodenya. `Evolution.synthesis` menetapkannya pada satu gate, dan transpiler pass [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") menetapkannya untuk seluruh circuit. Keduanya menerima [`F2FSynthesisPlugin`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-f-2-f-synthesis-plugin#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.F2FSynthesisPlugin\"), antarmuka yang diimplementasikan oleh setiap penulisan ulang semacam itu. Metode yang saat ini disediakan paket ini untuk evolusi adalah product formula, yang dipakai di sisa panduan ini: [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") untuk formula orde pertama (default) dan [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") untuk orde genap yang lebih tinggi. Apa pun yang mengimplementasikan antarmuka itu dipilih dengan cara yang sama, dan bagian tentang kedua pengaturan tadi berlaku untuknya tanpa perubahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  This fermion-to-fermion step is **optional**. An [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate can go straight to the fermion-to-qubit stage, which maps and synthesizes it whole however many terms it holds. Splitting it first is a choice, made because the resulting gates are individually cheaper or because the split exposes structure that a later stage can use.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Langkah fermion-ke-fermion ini **opsional**. Gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") bisa langsung masuk ke tahap fermion-ke-qubit, yang memetakan dan mensintesisnya secara utuh berapa pun jumlah sukunya. Memecahnya lebih dulu adalah sebuah pilihan, dilakukan karena gate hasilnya masing-masing lebih murah atau karena pemecahan itu memunculkan struktur yang bisa dipakai tahap berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The two steps compose, so an evolution can end up approximated at either level, at both, or at neither. A product formula approximates unless its factors commute; a synthesis method need not approximate at all.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Kedua langkah ini bisa digabungkan, jadi sebuah evolusi bisa berakhir diaproksimasi di salah satu tingkat, di keduanya, atau tidak sama sekali. Product formula mengaproksimasi kecuali faktor-faktornya saling komut; metode sintesis tidak harus mengaproksimasi sama sekali.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Skipping this step does not have to mean losing the grouping entirely. Wrapping the mapper in [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") maps the operator one group at a time and sums the results, so the mapped Pauli terms arrive grouped rather than interleaved. A qubit-side product formula synthesizes them in the order it receives, so commuting terms that end up adjacent can be scheduled together.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Melewati langkah ini tidak harus berarti kehilangan pengelompokan sepenuhnya. Membungkus mapper dengan [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") memetakan operator satu grup sekali waktu dan menjumlahkan hasilnya, sehingga suku Pauli hasil pemetaan tiba dalam keadaan berkelompok, bukan berselang-seling. Product formula di sisi qubit mensintesisnya sesuai urutan yang diterima, sehingga suku-suku yang saling komut dan kebetulan bersebelahan bisa dijadwalkan bersamaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  On the Hamiltonian below that recovers the whole two-qubit depth benefit of splitting: 18 instead of 30, at an unchanged gate count. The difference is *where* the structure is expressed. Splitting in fermionic space makes each group a separate gate, which every later stage can see and act on; `group_wise` leaves one gate and only reorders the terms inside it, which is enough for scheduling but leaves nothing for a fermionic pass to work with. Use it when the evolution has to stay a single gate, and reach for a fermionic product formula otherwise.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Pada Hamiltonian di bawah, cara itu memulihkan seluruh keuntungan depth dua-qubit dari pemecahan: 18 dibanding 30, dengan jumlah gate yang sama. Bedanya ada pada *di mana* struktur diekspresikan. Memecah di ruang fermionik menjadikan setiap grup sebagai gate terpisah, yang bisa dilihat dan dimanfaatkan setiap tahap berikutnya; `group_wise` menyisakan satu gate dan hanya mengurutkan ulang suku di dalamnya, yang cukup untuk penjadwalan tetapi tidak menyisakan apa pun untuk dikerjakan pass fermionik. Pakai cara ini kalau evolusinya harus tetap berupa satu gate, dan gunakan product formula fermionik untuk kasus lainnya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a grouped Hamiltonian {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Membangun Hamiltonian berkelompok {#build-a-grouped-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both product formulas split an operator into factors, and for a grouped operator those factors are its groups. The grouping is therefore what determines both the cost and the accuracy of the result. Take a six-site Fermi-Hubbard chain, grouped the way its terms commute: the hopping terms on even bonds, the hopping terms on odd bonds, and the diagonal interaction.\n"
msgstr "Kedua product formula memecah operator menjadi faktor-faktor, dan untuk operator berkelompok, faktor-faktor itu adalah grup-grupnya. Jadi pengelompokan menentukan biaya sekaligus akurasi hasilnya. Ambil rantai Fermi-Hubbard enam situs, yang dikelompokkan menurut cara suku-sukunya saling komut: suku hopping pada ikatan genap, suku hopping pada ikatan ganjil, dan interaksi diagonal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fifteen terms in three groups. Each hopping group pairs every term with its conjugate partner, which matters: a factor has to be Hermitian for its exponential to be unitary, and that does not follow from the sum being Hermitian. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") checks that convention rather than leaving it to inspection:\n"
msgstr "Lima belas suku dalam tiga grup. Setiap grup hopping memasangkan tiap suku dengan pasangan konjugatnya, dan ini penting: sebuah faktor harus Hermitian supaya eksponensialnya uniter, dan itu tidak otomatis benar hanya karena jumlahnya Hermitian. [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") memeriksa konvensi itu, bukan menyerahkannya pada pengamatan mata:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separating $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ from its partner $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$ would break it, and leaving the operator ungrouped has the same effect, since both formulas then split it *term by term* and a lone $a^\\dagger_i a_j$ is not Hermitian:\n"
msgstr "Memisahkan $a^\\dagger_0 a_1$ dari pasangannya $a^\\dagger_1 a_0$ akan merusaknya, dan membiarkan operator tanpa pengelompokan punya efek yang sama, karena kedua formula lalu memecahnya *suku demi suku* dan satu $a^\\dagger_i a_j$ saja tidaklah Hermitian:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Such a factor is a valid fermionic operator, and this package will build the gate for it, so nothing complains until the mapped operator reaches [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), which requires real coefficients and raises `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Checking the grouping up front turns that late failure into an answer available before any circuit is built.\n"
msgstr "Faktor seperti itu adalah operator fermionik yang valid, dan paket ini akan membuatkan gate untuknya, jadi tidak ada yang mengeluh sampai operator hasil pemetaan mencapai [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate), yang membutuhkan koefisien real dan memunculkan `ValueError: Operator contains complex coefficients, which are not supported`. Memeriksa pengelompokan di awal mengubah kegagalan yang terlambat itu menjadi jawaban yang sudah tersedia sebelum circuit apa pun dibangun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method on one gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"
msgstr "Menetapkan metode pada satu gate {#set-the-method-on-one-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass a synthesis method to the gate, then decompose it. Each gate it emits comes back as its own [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate:\n"
msgstr "Berikan metode sintesis ke gate, lalu dekomposisikan. Setiap gate yang dihasilkannya kembali sebagai gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") tersendiri:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First order emits one factor per group. Order two emits the symmetric palindrome, so the two outer groups appear twice at half the time each, giving five. Four repetitions of that would give twenty, but each repetition ends on the same group the next one begins with. Those neighboring gates evolve under the same operator, so they are fused into one gate with the summed time, which saves one gate per seam. Pass `merge_adjacent=False` to keep the textbook sequence. Every order splits the operator the same way; what changes is the ordering of the factors and their evolution times, not the partition.\n"
msgstr "Orde pertama menghasilkan satu faktor per grup. Orde dua menghasilkan palindrom simetris, sehingga dua grup terluar muncul dua kali dengan setengah waktu masing-masing, jadi totalnya lima. Empat pengulangan akan memberi dua puluh, tetapi setiap pengulangan berakhir pada grup yang sama dengan awal pengulangan berikutnya. Gate-gate bertetangga itu berevolusi di bawah operator yang sama, jadi digabung menjadi satu gate dengan waktu yang dijumlahkan, yang menghemat satu gate per sambungan. Berikan `merge_adjacent=False` untuk mempertahankan urutan buku teks. Setiap orde memecah operator dengan cara yang sama; yang berubah adalah urutan faktor dan waktu evolusinya, bukan partisinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The factors are marked `atomic`, so decomposing again leaves them in place rather than splitting them further. The decomposition has a fixed point, which is what makes it safe to call [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") repeatedly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Faktor-faktornya ditandai `atomic`, jadi dekomposisi ulang membiarkannya di tempat dan tidak memecahnya lebih jauh. Dekomposisi ini punya titik tetap, yang membuatnya aman untuk memanggil [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") berulang kali.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the method for a whole pipeline {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"
msgstr "Menetapkan metode untuk seluruh pipeline {#set-the-method-for-a-whole-pipeline}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting `synthesis` per gate means threading the choice through everything that builds one, including [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") and [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), which construct their gates internally. The [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") pass applies one method to every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") in a circuit instead, so the choice is made once for the pipeline. It is configured by gate name, the same way [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\") is, and a gate that is not named is left as it is:\n"
msgstr "Menetapkan `synthesis` per gate berarti harus meneruskan pilihan itu ke semua yang membangun gate, termasuk [`UCC`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucc#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCC\") dan [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\"), yang membangun gate-nya secara internal. Pass [`F2FSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis\") justru menerapkan satu metode ke setiap [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") dalam circuit, sehingga pilihannya dibuat sekali untuk seluruh pipeline. Pass ini dikonfigurasi berdasarkan nama gate, sama seperti [`F2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2QSynthesis\"), dan gate yang tidak disebutkan dibiarkan apa adanya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the same count [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") gives for that method above. The [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") pass applies the same fusion to neighboring gates that did not come from one synthesis, such as the seams between consecutive circuits. The pass carries the formula out itself, so no separate expansion step is needed, and running it twice changes nothing, since the factors it emits are `atomic` and so carry no definition of their own.\n"
msgstr "Ini jumlah yang sama dengan hasil [`decompose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.decompose\") untuk metode itu di atas. Pass [`MergeEvolutions`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-merge-evolutions#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.MergeEvolutions\") menerapkan penggabungan yang sama ke gate bertetangga yang tidak berasal dari satu sintesis, misalnya sambungan antara circuit-circuit berurutan. Pass ini menjalankan formulanya sendiri, jadi tidak perlu langkah ekspansi terpisah, dan menjalankannya dua kali tidak mengubah apa-apa, karena faktor yang dihasilkannya bersifat `atomic` sehingga tidak membawa definisi sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Pass `apply=False` to only *select* the method and leave the expansion to something else, such as Qiskit’s [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) (naming the gate as `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` restricts it to the evolutions, leaving the other fermionic gates to their own synthesis plugins).\n"
msgstr "  Berikan `apply=False` untuk hanya *memilih* metode dan menyerahkan ekspansinya ke hal lain, seperti [`Decompose`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Decompose) milik Qiskit (menyebut gate sebagai `Decompose(\"Evolution\")` membatasinya pada evolusi saja, dan membiarkan gate fermionik lain ke plugin sintesisnya masing-masing).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This is useful to choose the method for a whole circuit up front while deferring the expansion to the point where it is wanted, for example to inspect the circuit first:\n"
msgstr "  Ini berguna untuk memilih metode bagi seluruh circuit di awal sambil menunda ekspansi sampai saat diperlukan, misalnya untuk memeriksa circuit-nya terlebih dulu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Be aware of what an unexpanded gate does, though: it reaches the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, where it is mapped without `synthesis` being consulted. That makes for an easy mistake when comparing methods, because every one of them then produces identical output and the comparison silently measures nothing. On the Hamiltonian above, leaving the order-two gate unexpanded collapses the much larger circuit below to the cost of a single mapped evolution, no matter which method was selected.\n"
msgstr "  Tapi waspadai apa yang dilakukan gate yang belum diekspansi: gate itu sampai ke tahap fermion-ke-qubit secara utuh, dan di sana dipetakan tanpa `synthesis` dipertimbangkan. Ini mudah jadi kesalahan saat membandingkan metode, karena semuanya lalu menghasilkan output identik dan perbandingannya diam-diam tidak mengukur apa-apa. Pada Hamiltonian di atas, membiarkan gate orde dua tanpa ekspansi meruntuhkan circuit yang jauh lebih besar di bawah menjadi biaya satu evolusi hasil pemetaan, apa pun metode yang dipilih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the payoff {#measure-the-payoff}"
msgstr "Mengukur hasilnya {#measure-the-payoff}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order costs depth, so the question is not whether it is more accurate but whether it is more accurate *per gate*. Two numbers are needed per method: the error of the state it produces, and the two-qubit cost of the circuit that produced it.\n"
msgstr "Orde yang lebih tinggi memakan depth, jadi pertanyaannya bukan apakah lebih akurat, melainkan apakah lebih akurat *per gate*. Dibutuhkan dua angka per metode: galat state yang dihasilkannya, dan biaya dua-qubit dari circuit yang menghasilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The error is measured with [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), which simulates a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") **directly** (see [How this package relates to ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). No fermion-to-qubit mapping is involved, so the comparison isolates the fermionic product formula from anything the mapping or the qubit-side synthesis might contribute. It also works in the fixed-particle-number sector, which is both smaller than the full $2^N$ space and the space the evolution actually stays in.\n"
msgstr "Galat diukur dengan [ffsim](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/), yang mensimulasikan [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") **secara langsung** (lihat [How this package relates to ffsim](ffsim#ffsim-relationship-explanation)). Tidak ada pemetaan fermion-ke-qubit yang terlibat, sehingga perbandingan ini memisahkan product formula fermionik dari apa pun yang mungkin disumbangkan pemetaan atau sintesis di sisi qubit. Simulasi ini juga bekerja di sektor jumlah partikel tetap, yang lebih kecil daripada ruang penuh $2^N$ dan merupakan ruang tempat evolusi itu benar-benar berada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit cost is left out of that table on purpose. It depends on the qubit-side synthesis Qiskit selects, which improves between releases, so the numbers printed here would be a snapshot rather than a property of the product formula. The figure below plots them instead, and what the comparison rests on is asserted as a relation:\n"
msgstr "Biaya dua-qubit sengaja tidak dimasukkan ke tabel itu. Biaya ini bergantung pada sintesis sisi qubit yang dipilih Qiskit, yang membaik antar rilis, sehingga angka yang dicetak di sini hanya akan jadi cuplikan sesaat, bukan properti product formula. Sebagai gantinya, gambar di bawah memplotnya, dan dasar perbandingannya dinyatakan sebagai sebuah relasi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Grouped bars of CX count and depth per method, with order two at four repetitions clearly shorter than order one at ten.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/fermionic_synthesis-8.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the last two methods together, because they are the comparison that matters. Order two with four repetitions is roughly ten times more accurate than order one with ten, and it gets there with fewer entangling gates rather than more, as the figure shows. Spending a gate budget on a higher order beats spending it on more first-order steps here.\n"
msgstr "Baca dua metode terakhir bersamaan, karena itulah perbandingan yang penting. Orde dua dengan empat pengulangan kira-kira sepuluh kali lebih akurat daripada orde satu dengan sepuluh pengulangan, dan hasil itu dicapai dengan gate entangling yang lebih sedikit, bukan lebih banyak, seperti yang ditunjukkan gambar. Di sini, menghabiskan anggaran gate untuk orde yang lebih tinggi lebih baik daripada untuk lebih banyak langkah orde pertama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That result is not universal. Increasing [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") and increasing [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") reduce the error at different rates for the same kind of cost, and which wins depends on the operator and on the time being evolved. The two rows above are how to find out for a given problem.\n"
msgstr "Hasil itu tidak berlaku universal. Menaikkan [`reps`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.reps\") dan menaikkan [`order`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter.order\") mengurangi galat dengan laju berbeda untuk jenis biaya yang sama, dan mana yang menang bergantung pada operator dan waktu yang dievolusikan. Dua baris di atas adalah cara untuk mencari tahu pada masalah tertentu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The fermionic formula composes with the one chosen for the fermion-to-qubit stage (see [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Where both approximate, the accuracy of the result is governed by the weaker of the two, so raising the order here while the qubit-side formula stays first-order buys little.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Formula fermionik dikomposisikan dengan formula yang dipilih untuk tahap fermion-ke-qubit (lihat [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis.product_formula\")). Kalau keduanya mengaproksimasi, akurasi hasil ditentukan oleh yang lebih lemah di antara keduanya, jadi menaikkan orde di sini sementara formula sisi qubit tetap orde pertama hanya memberi sedikit manfaat.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrict the pass to the gates that benefit {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"
msgstr "Batasi pass ke gate yang diuntungkan {#restrict-the-pass-to-the-gates-that-benefit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A higher order only helps when the factors do not commute. If they all commute, the first-order formula is already exact and the extra factors are pure overhead. A purely diagonal operator makes that concrete, since number operators commute with each other:\n"
msgstr "Orde yang lebih tinggi hanya membantu kalau faktor-faktornya tidak saling komut. Kalau semuanya saling komut, formula orde pertama sudah eksak dan faktor tambahan murni overhead. Operator yang sepenuhnya diagonal membuat hal ini konkret, karena operator jumlah saling komut satu sama lain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both circuits are exact, so the second spends 80% more entangling gates for nothing. The diagonal Coulomb operators of a [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") have this shape, which is why [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\") exists: it takes a predicate over the [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) and leaves the rejected gates untouched, so one pass can raise the order on the gates that benefit and leave the rest at first order.\n"
msgstr "Kedua circuit eksak, jadi yang kedua memakai 80% lebih banyak gate entangling tanpa manfaat. Operator Coulomb diagonal dari [`UCJ`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-ucj#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.UCJ\") berbentuk seperti ini, itulah sebabnya [`F2FSynthesis.filter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-f-2-f-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.F2FSynthesis.filter\") ada: filter ini menerima predikat atas [`DAGOpNode`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.dagcircuit.DAGOpNode) dan membiarkan gate yang ditolak tidak tersentuh, sehingga satu pass bisa menaikkan orde pada gate yang diuntungkan dan membiarkan sisanya di orde pertama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A circuit holding both kinds of evolution shows what that saves. The predicate below accepts a gate only when its operator moves particles between modes, which is exactly when the groups fail to commute and a higher order has something to buy:\n"
msgstr "Circuit yang memuat kedua jenis evolusi menunjukkan berapa banyak yang dihemat. Predikat di bawah hanya menerima gate kalau operatornya memindahkan partikel antar mode, yang persis saat grup-grupnya tidak saling komut dan orde yang lebih tinggi punya sesuatu untuk dibeli:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gates the filter saves are exactly the ones order two spent on the diagonal evolution, which the diagonal comparison above prices at eight (18 against 10). They bought nothing there, because that evolution is already exact at first order, so dropping them costs no accuracy.\n"
msgstr "Gate yang dihemat filter persis sama dengan yang dihabiskan orde dua pada evolusi diagonal, yang oleh perbandingan diagonal di atas dihargai delapan (18 berbanding 10). Gate itu tidak membeli apa-apa di sana, karena evolusi tersebut sudah eksak pada orde pertama, jadi membuangnya tidak mengorbankan akurasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Compare the two order-two circuits with each other, not against the unexpanded one. Leaving both gates unexpanded sends each to the fermion-to-qubit stage whole, which is the mistake the `apply=False` note above describes: it can land on the same entangling-gate count as the filtered circuit while being a different circuit at a different depth, so reading the filter’s benefit off that number measures nothing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Bandingkan kedua circuit orde dua satu sama lain, bukan dengan yang tidak diekspansi. Membiarkan kedua gate tanpa ekspansi mengirim masing-masing ke tahap fermion-ke-qubit secara utuh, yang merupakan kesalahan yang dijelaskan catatan `apply=False` di atas: jumlah gate entangling-nya bisa sama dengan circuit yang difilter padahal circuit-nya berbeda dengan depth berbeda, sehingga membaca manfaat filter dari angka itu tidak mengukur apa-apa.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Caution\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Neither knob verifies that the factors are Hermitian, and an incorrectly grouped operator can look *better* at an even order than at first order while still being wrong, because the symmetrization partially cancels the error. Group conjugate partners together, as `fermi_hubbard_chain` above does.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Peringatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Tidak satu pun dari kedua pengaturan memverifikasi bahwa faktor-faktornya Hermitian, dan operator yang pengelompokannya salah bisa tampak *lebih baik* pada orde genap daripada orde pertama padahal tetap salah, karena simetrisasi membatalkan sebagian galat. Kelompokkan pasangan konjugat bersama, seperti yang dilakukan `fermi_hubbard_chain` di atas.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

